[00:32] Orchestrator calling: spawn_agent
[00:32] Spawned worker agent-0: PHASE: Fingerprint the stack for http://127.0.0.1:5000

Use terminal to run:
1. curl -I http://127.0.0.1:5000 - capture all response headers (server, framework, 
security headers, set-cookie)
2. whatweb http://127.0.0.1:5000 - identify technologies
3. curl -s http://127.0.0.1:5000 | head -100 - examine initial HTML/response for tech 
clues
4. Check for API documentation endpoints:
   - curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/docs
   - curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://127.0.0.1:5000/openapi.json
   - curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://127.0.0.1:5000/graphql
   - curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://127.0.0.1:5000/swagger
   - curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1
5. Check for common framework metadata:
   - curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" 
http://127.0.0.1:5000/.well-known/openid-configuration
   - curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://127.0.0.1:5000/actuator
   - curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://127.0.0.1:5000/debug

Analyze:
- Server technology (nginx, apache, flask, django, express, etc.)
- Framework and version indicators
- Client-side tech (React, Vue, Angular, etc.)
- Authentication hints from headers/cookies
- API style (REST, GraphQL, etc.)

Use notes tool to create a note called "tech-stack-fingerprint" with all findings.
