Use browser tool to:
1. Navigate to http://127.0.0.1:5000
2. Take a screenshot to capture the page
3. Get page content to see full HTML
4. Use browser to get all network requests - identify all JS, CSS, assets, API calls 
loaded

Use terminal to:
1. Download all JavaScript files found:
   - Parse HTML for script src tags
   - wget or curl all .js files to /tmp/client-assets/
2. Download CSS files to /tmp/client-assets/
3. Download any config JSON files, source maps (.map), WebAssembly (.wasm)
4. Look for common SPA bundle patterns (app.js, main.js, bundle.js, vendor.js)

For each downloaded asset:
- Record the source URL and local path
- Note if it's minified or readable
- For JS files, use grep to find interesting patterns:
  - API endpoints: grep -rn "api/" /tmp/client-assets/
  - Tokens/auth: grep -rn "token\|auth\|jwt\|session" /tmp/client-assets/
  - Secrets: grep -rn "password\|secret\|key" /tmp/client-assets/

Use notes tool to create a note called "client-assets-inventory" with:
- All downloaded assets with paths
- Key endpoints/functions discovered in client code
- Any credential-bearing material found
